## Features

### Customer
- Discover nearby facilities via location-based search
- View courts and a real-time slot availability grid
- Book a slot and pay online through Razorpay
- View booking history and cancel bookings
- Join a waitlist for full slots (notified by email if one opens up)

### Owner
- Create and manage multiple facilities with image uploads
- Add courts and bulk-generate time slots for a date range
- View bookings and an analytics dashboard (revenue, occupancy trends)
- Delete courts/facilities with password re-verification for facility deletion

### Platform
- Role-based access (`OWNER` / `CUSTOMER`)
- Real-time slot updates across all connected clients
- Concurrency-safe booking — no double-booking under simultaneous requests

## Tech Stack

| Layer | Technology |
|---|---|
| Frontend | React (Vite), React Router, TanStack Query, Tailwind CSS, Leaflet, Recharts, Socket.io-client |
| Backend | Node.js, Express, Socket.io |
| Database | PostgreSQL, Prisma ORM |
| Authentication | JWT (access + refresh tokens) |
| Payments | Razorpay |
| Storage | Cloudinary (image uploads) |
| Email | EmailJS |
| Maps/Location | Leaflet + OpenStreetMap Nominatim (geocoding), Haversine-based distance search |
| Deployment | Vercel (frontend) | Render (Backend)

## Key Technical Highlights

- **Concurrency-safe slot locking** — booking a slot uses an atomic `updateMany` that only succeeds if the slot is still `AVAILABLE`. When multiple requests race for the same slot, exactly one succeeds and the rest fail cleanly, preventing double-booking without needing a database lock.
- **JWT auth with refresh-token rotation** — short-lived access tokens paired with refresh tokens that are hashed before storage and reissued on every refresh, so a leaked token has a short useful life.
- **Role-based authorization** — middleware restricts routes by `OWNER`/`CUSTOMER` role, and controllers additionally check resource ownership (e.g. an owner can only edit their own facilities).
- **Verified payments** — after Razorpay checkout, the backend recomputes the HMAC-SHA256 signature server-side and only confirms the booking if it matches, rather than trusting the client.
- **Real-time updates** — Socket.io broadcasts slot status changes, so a slot booked by one user visibly locks for everyone else viewing the same facility, without a page refresh.
- **Time-zone-aware slot logic** — slot start times are compared in IST (Asia/Kolkata) on both frontend and backend so "past" slots are disabled correctly regardless of server timezone.
- **Relational integrity** — a `Booking` has a unique constraint on `slotId` (one booking per slot at the DB level), and a `Waitlist` entry is unique per `[slotId, userId]`.

## System Architecture

```
React Client (Vite)
      │
      ├── REST API ────────► Node.js + Express
      │                            │
      └── WebSocket (Socket.io) ◄──┤
                                   Prisma ORM
                                    │
                              PostgreSQL

External services: Razorpay (payments), Cloudinary (image storage), EmailJS (transactional email)
```

## Booking Flow

```
Select Slot
   │
   ▼
Lock Slot (atomic update: AVAILABLE → LOCKED)
   │
   ▼
Create Razorpay Order
   │
   ▼
Razorpay Checkout
   │
   ▼
Verify Payment Signature (HMAC-SHA256)
   │
   ▼
Confirm Booking (slot → BOOKED, payment → PAID)
   │
   ▼
Real-time Slot Update (Socket.io)
   │
   ▼
Email Notification (customer + owner)
```

If the customer abandons checkout, the pending booking is deleted and the slot returns to `AVAILABLE`.

## Database Design

```
User
├── Facility (owner)
│     └── Court
│           └── Slot
│                 ├── Booking
│                 │     └── Payment
│                 └── Waitlist
└── Booking / Waitlist (customer)
```

